    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d49">

                <pb facs="0116" n="48" sameAs="frus:frus1914-20v01/pg48"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">362.412 C31/1</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Belgium</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Whitlock</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 186</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Brussels</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-10-19">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 19, 1915</hi>.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 5.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit herewith
                    enclosed for the information and files of the Department copies of
                    correspondence with the Ambassador at London and with the German Government of
                    Occupation in Belgium in regard to the case of Miss Edith Cavell, an English
                    woman, who was executed last week for assisting soldiers to reach the Dutch
                    frontier.</p>
                <p>Further than saying that the Legation exhausted every effort to prevent the
                    infliction of the death penalty, I make no comment upon the facts in this case
                    which are fully shown by the correspondence itself.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d49-f1"
                    />
                </p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Brand Whitlock</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>











